xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:1:**VERDICT: SOUND — Q/max is the unique uniform repair of Notation 3.5; Q plus printed Statement 3.17(ii) and Proposition 9.3(e) force E5; CONJECTURE \(U_{7C}\) is a new assertion that no printed or promoted fact in the audited chain proves; the 17-cell Q+E5 book is the sound conservative object under the filed census perimeter.**
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:5:Claims under review: (1) P/coarse at a doubly realized vertex is incoherent — it yields nonintegral \(D_{h,F}=\kappa_F d_{h,F}\), contradicting printed Statement 3.8, and conflicts with Proposition 5.5 — hence Q/jump/max \(\kappa_F=\nu_F\kappa_G/\nu_G\) is forced; (2) Q forces the E5 transport identities via printed Statement 3.17(ii) + Proposition 9.3(e), so the printed \(\nu_F\) denominators in Proposition 9.3(g),(h) are wrong unless \(\nu_F=\nu_G\); (3) the 2-cell book needs a new assertion CONJECTURE \(U_{7C}\) (\(\nu_F=\nu_G\) on the relevant case-III edges), which no printed/promoted fact proves; an exact polynomial model shows the definitions permit \(\nu_F\neq\nu_G\) (not a Keller pair, so \(U_{7C}\) is not refuted). Consequence: 17-cell book = sound conservative object.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:7:Method: printed pages 12–14, 17–18, 26–27, 40–42, 49–60 extracted with `pdftotext` from `refs/sigray_full.pdf`; independent exact `Fraction` chart calculus, Wronskian leftover, and Jacobian of the model (no sympy); 69-row rational SAT prefix substituted term-by-term; `px2.chain_steps` / `px5.close_with_cells` replay of the discriminating path; line-read of SHEET6-III, SHEET6-HIII-REVIEW, SIGRAY-AUDIT, BOOK-OFFAXIS §11a, FLEET.md, AUDIT.md parenthesis/mod-p rules.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:39:  **Proposition 5.5 independently forces Q at poles.** Printed p.26 boxed (18): \(\Lambda(P)=D_{g,F}/\nu_F\) if \(c=0\), and \(=D_{g,F}\) if \(c\neq 0\). Printed \(c=0\) proof (p.27): \(P\) has \(\alpha_m<u\); any other \(Q\) realizing \(F\) has characteristics \((\nu_F\kappa,\beta_1,\ldots,\beta_m,u)\); then \(\Lambda(P)=\kappa d_{g,F}=D_F/\nu_F\). Together with \(D_{g,F}=\kappa_F d_{g,F}\) this is \(\kappa_F=\nu_F\kappa\), the Q-value. P-value \(\kappa_F=\kappa\) would make the displayed equality \(\kappa d=(\kappa d)/\nu_F\), false at a pole. The dropped \(g\)-subscripts are the already audited Proposition 5.5 typo; boxed (18) carries the correct subscript. Scope is exactly the in-context \(c=0\) pole case the note claims — it does **not** by itself force Q at a nonpole class-C merge. The note already records that caveat.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:43:  **What is forced.** Among the two Notation 3.5 presentation-values, only Q/max is a uniform global convention compatible with printed Statement 3.8, with the integer \(\bar\kappa\) the thesis itself uses (Statement 9.4 p.49: \(\kappa_G(\pi(G)-1)\in\mathbb N\); every printed Q-datum in 9.6–9.11), and with Proposition 5.5 at poles. A P-only-at-nonpole-III split is not refuted by a pre-§9 pointwise theorem; it is also not a reading Notation 3.5 supplies, and it is unusable by the promoted integer Q-data/N1 book. The note does not overclaim this.
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:96:- Claim: the 2-cell book requires CONJECTURE \(U_{7C}\); no independently justified printed or promoted fact proves it; the local model has \(\nu_F=3\neq 2=\nu_G\) and satisfies the isolated local hypotheses; it is not a Keller pair, so it does not refute \(U_{7C}\).
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:110:  **No other printed/promoted equality theorem in the audited chain.** SHEET6-III files E5 as an erratum and records the printed-literal alternative \(\nu_F=\nu_G\) as a *reading*, not a derivation. HIII-REVIEW Front 3 confirms both coherent readings give the same \(\lambda\)-bound and that “no printed computation discriminates.” SIGRAY-AUDIT upgrades H5a via Statement 3.8; it does not mention index equality. BOOK-OFFAXIS §11a records both books and does not prove the restriction. N1, AF2, P0/P3, St 8.2/8.4/8.5 (8.5 is inapplicable because the case-III parent lies in \(V_{2,a}\)), St 5.2, and St 6.2 do not force \(\nu_F=\nu_G\).
xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:125:  **Consequence.** Deleting the 15 unequal-index cells requires \(U_{7C}\). Without it, the conservative work queue under the filed P0/P3/arrival/closure/budget hypotheses is the promoted 17-cell / 238 raw / 233 dedup book at `BOOK-OFFAXIS.md:750`. The 2-cell / 49 dedup restriction at `:790` is the sub-book after adjoining \(U_{7C}\). Census numbers were not re-enumerated here; they were already hostile-replayed in `xmodel/grok-census11a-review.md`. “Unconditionally” in the review prompt overstates the note: the 17-cell *count* is perimeter-conditional; what is unconditional relative to the printed thesis plus Q is that the 15 cells cannot be killed at the proved tier.
