xmodel/grok-td11-review.md:82:  **`v_2` is identity, not a stack-length fact.** `v_2(8) = 3`. A `w = 3` prefix `A` is 3-free and may be even (`ν = 2` is legal); extra 2-adic valuation only enlarges the left side. A `w = 2` suffix `B` is odd, so `v_2(B) = 0`. Chain-1 is frozen at `M = 1`, `μ = 1`, `Pi` odd, `v_2(2·Pi) = 1`. Replayed on all stacks of length `≤ 2` with letters `< 40`: zero failures. The promoted certificate at `sol-normalform.md:584–599` is exactly this comparison and assumes `μ = (1,1)`, which the drop now forces.
xmodel/grok-td11-review.md:92:  **Death equation is the promoted one.** `ℓ/k = gap(X) + α − 1`. Existence of integers `ℓ, k` with `k | c` is equivalent to `c · r ∈ ℤ`, i.e. `den(r) | c`. Confirmed against the Case C display `ℓ_m/k_m = α_m − 1/2 + 1/(2ν_X)`.
